continuing with the idea of getting the takuya effects to display the pressed keys on the oled, i pondered about the idea of showing the last letter pressed on the master layer, but the default font it's too small, an entire typography is needed for a size that is actually visible (32x32), i leave it for later, also decided to continue the customization and extend the weyland-yutani theme to the master screen

in some customizations, there are a cozy information screen with a bunch of stuff: 4 icons shown with the 4 modifiers that you find on mac, a wpm counter etc, i come up with the idea of replacing them with the semiotic icons of alien1 again, the information it's lost but that's the point of alien1 and i really like the idea anyway, so made the icons on photoshop and then decide to change everything else on the screen and reference alien1: the wpm is now the self-destruct screen with the animated cross, the last letter pressed is microgramma typography etc

still embedded of the takuya spirit, i realize that no matter how i put the elements, they don't look good, they are too big and too few to look 'right', i remove everything except the icons which i like, and realize that instead of 4, i could fill the entire screen with icons, the original concept have 2 dozens to choose from, so i make a photoshop test image and the result is incredible, i'm fascinated with the result

spend all day designing the entire original set, then debugging a serious roadblock when some icons turn out corrupt, just to discover hours after that qmk interprets such letter positions as line returns, which corrupts the screen, finally, after recreating the entire graphics of the font, i decide that i've already fought gemini enough to stop writting letters when we are writing icons instead, so i write the screen drawing routine by hand, and when the oled screen finally shows all the icons correctly i marvel myself and go to sleep at 3am
